# Context

## Background
The oal bin (apps/cli/src/index.ts, #!/usr/bin/env node) runs through
Node 24.18 type stripping. Node enables strip-only mode for the CLI
entry, which accepts erasable syntax only and throws
ERR_UNSUPPORTED_TYPESCRIPT_SYNTAX on parameter properties.

## Why This Way
Every earlier test ran through vitest or main() in-process, which
compiles through esbuild and erases parameter properties silently.
The first live `oal run` through a real node process exposed the gap.

## Gotchas
- Single-line and multi-line constructor signatures both hide these;
  the reliable scanner is a regex over the raw source:
  /constructor\([^)]*?\b(?:private|public|protected)\b[^)]*?\)/gs
- Bare `readonly` constructor parameters (no access modifier) are also
  rejected by strip-only mode.
- `readonly string[]` and `readonly SourceLine[]` array types and
  readonly inside option-object types are false positives.

